<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fall of Singapore</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a> was the surrender of the British garrison to Japanese forces in February 1942, after a rapid campaign through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaya">Malaya</a>. It was one of the greatest triumphs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and a severe blow to British imperial prestige in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fall-of-singapore.jpg" alt="Fall of Singapore" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photographer not identified. &quot;Official photograph&quot;. Post-Work: W.wolny · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Surrender_Singapore.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
